      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Herewith we report a case of redo coronary-surgery which was approached through a left thoracotomy and in hypothermic arrest so as to avoid either a demanding dissection with its potential consequences over the functioning grafts and aortic cross-clamping thus making unnecessary any cardioplegia delivery. We describe the surgical procedure and analyze its advantages with respect to the usual median sternotomy approach."},
